# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every OS (audit I-6): the tests parse workflow files, scripts
# and generated JSON, and Windows' CRLF would make them fail on a PC. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Never touched.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
